[h1]Cybernetic Creed Synod (4.5)[/h1]

Because the cybernetic creeds are really cool, surely the galaxy is big enough for all of them?

I was always disappointed that all the cool flavour of the creeds, their demands and their cool buildings would disappear 20 years into the game as you rush cybernetic ascension.  So I wrote this mod to make them a larger part of the game.

This adds a new option to the Cybernetic Creed Origin: The Galaxy is large enough for All Creeds - your empire will go forward with all 4 creeds and they will learn to work together.

You will be able to build and destroy the individual creed buildings, as well as the temple of the united creeds.

[h1]Faction Updates[/h1]
If you take the option for all 4 creeds, then the Creeds themselves will need to decide what they mean in the new universe:
[list]
[*][b]The Fellowship of the Hammer[/b]: will focus on whether Xenos are welcome or not in the fellowship, becoming [i]Xenophile[/i] or [i]Xenophobe[/i]
[*][b]The Templars of Steel[/b]: will focus on the nature of war itself: for self defence only or for glorious conquest, becoming [i]Pacifist[/i] or [i]Militarist[/i]
[*][b]The Commune of Toil[/b]: about the place of toilers in society itself becoming [i]Egalitarian[/i] or [i]Authoritarian[/i]
[*][b]The Choir of the Mind[/b]: will try to answer the question about whether robots have a soul, while they will remain [i]Spiritualist[/i] they can gain [i]Materialist[/i] demands.
[/list]
This is in addition to how you treated them before the creeds united -the creeds absolutely remember who you favoured, and will hold it against you for the entire game.


[h1]Planet Dedication[/h1]
You can dedicate a planet to a specific creed, and you better bet that the Creed factions want to be the one with the most planets dedicated to them.  Balancing who has the most shiny toys is now a faction problem.

If you dedicate a planet to a creed you can build that creed's buildings on the planet, and only that creed's buildings.

You can instead declare a planet as belonging to all creeds, letting you build the buildings of all the creeds, but there is a catch, just because the creeds agreed to work together, doesn't mean that they like sharing, for every creed building after the first you will receive a stability penalty and an efficiency penalty to rulers and unity producers as you have to dedicate resources to stop the creeds from squabbling.

Your capital does not have this problem, all creeds agree to respect the sanctity of the capital, and the temples of the united creeds are declared as neutral ground that do not cause penalties.

